# The account and the secrets of polaris. Copy this file to .env and fill in the
# values there. Git ignores .env but keeps this file, so never write values here.
#
# `cf dev` reads .env. `pnpm stack:deploy` deploys polaris to the account below and
# uploads these values to the Worker as secrets. Keep other credentials, such as a
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN for cf itself, out of this file.

# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#   The Cloudflare account that polaris watches. cf deploys the Worker to this
#   account.
#   `cf accounts list` shows the IDs of your accounts.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN
#   A Cloudflare API token that reads the usage of the account above.
#   It belongs to the account rather than to a person, and it can only read.
#
#   To issue it:
#   1. Open this link. It opens the form for a new account API token, with the
#      name "polaris" and the seven read permissions below selected.
#      https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/api-tokens&permissionGroupKeys=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22account_analytics%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22d1%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22da1261c3d38544a4bba805b22566f8b6%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%227cf72faf220841aabcfdfab81c43c4f6%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22workers_kv_storage%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22queues%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22query_cache%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%5D&name=polaris
#   2. If Cloudflare asks for an account, choose the account of CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID.
#   3. Account Analytics Read, D1 Read, Workers Metadata Read-Only, and Billing Read
#      are required.
#      Workers KV Storage Read, Queues Read, and Hyperdrive Read are optional and let
#      the dashboards show resource names instead of IDs. Remove any optional
#      permissions you do not need, then select "Continue to summary" and "Create Token".
#   4. Copy the token, which Cloudflare shows only once, and paste it after
#      ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN= below.
#
#   To replace it, issue a new token the same way, paste it here, deploy again,
#   and delete the old token on the Account API Tokens page of the account.
ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN=
